{"id":"u-51bdc7be-e6f9-40e7-9dea-88791112edbf","src":"community","title":"Guts PPLWP","author":"Daven L.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/YHf98q-guts-pplwp","desc":"🔹 Progression Rules in  5×5\n\nAdd weight each workout\n\nSquat: +5 lb (2.5 kg) every workout\n\nBench Press, Overhead Press, Barbell Row: +5 lb (2.5 kg) every workout\n\nDeadlift: +10 lb (5 kg) every workout\n\n→ Since you train 3x/week, this adds up to ~15 lb/week on squats and ~30 lb/week on deadlifts in the early stages.\n\nIf you fail a lift (can’t get 5×5 with good form):\n\nRetry the same weight at your next session.\n\nIf you fail 3 times in a row, deload (reduce the weight by 10%) and build back up.\n\nDeloads are part of the plan\nThey allow recovery and give you momentum to break past sticking points. The idea is you’ll come back stronger after a reset.\n\nWhen it gets really heavy\n\nYou’ll eventually stop being able to add weight every workout.\n\nAt that point, the program suggests switching to 3×5 instead of 5×5 to reduce fatigue and allow progress.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":3,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-03-18T07:54:36.000Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["PULL #1","PUSH #1","LEGS #1","WP & ARMS #1"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":5,"x":5}]},{"n":"Dumbbell Row","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":5,"x":3}],"note":"flaired out elbow"},{"n":"Pullover (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Rear Delt Fly (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":2.5,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":5,"x":5}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Chest Fly (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Skull Crusher